{"name":"Buzz-In","hex":"#ffd756","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"buzz","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A continuous humming noise, as of bees; a confused murmur, as of general conversation in low tones.","A whisper."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a low, continuous, humming or sibilant sound, like that made by bees with their wings.\n\n To utter a murmuring sound; to speak with a low, humming voice.\n\nOf a group of people, to talk about some interesting topic excitedly.\n\n To fly while making such a sound.","To utter a murmuring sound; to speak with a low, humming voice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buzz"}],"entries":[],"images":[],"sounds":{"buzz":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/En-us-buzz.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/0c/En-us-buzz.ogg/En-us-buzz.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5d/Electronic_Alarmclocksound.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5d/Electronic_Alarmclocksound.ogg/Electronic_Alarmclocksound.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Etymology of a Classical Meitei language term for “yellow colour”","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Etymology_of_a_Classical_Meitei_language_term_for_%E2%80%9Cyellow_colour%E2%80%9D.jpg/500px-Etymology_of_a_Classical_Meitei_language_term_for_%E2%80%9Cyellow_colour%E2%80%9D.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Etymology_of_a_Classical_Meitei_language_term_for_%E2%80%9Cyellow_colour%E2%80%9D.jpg","share":0.616875},{"title":"Yellow Portulaca flower in sunshine, on black background","image":"https:/